  A violation compile: a library-shaped project whose every marked line breaks a rule the build claims
  to enforce. It is NOT in Zabbix.slnx and is expected to fail; DesignConformanceTests builds it and holds each
  `// expect: ID` mark to the error the build reports at that line. It is analysed as a library: the solution's
  Directory.Build.* (through the props below), .editorconfig and BannedSymbols.txt, none of the test relaxations.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <RootNamespace>Community.Zabbix.Analyzers</RootNamespace>
    <!-- Not a real library surface, so it opts out of Directory.Build.targets' PublicApiAnalyzers
         wiring the same way tools/Zabbix.PowerShell.HelpGen does — this project has no PublicAPI.Shipped/Unshipped.txt
         and is not meant to grow one; every marked line already fails on purpose, and RS0016/RS0037 firing on every
         OTHER symbol here (there is no baseline file at all) drowned out The_probe_build_fails_only_where_a_probe_is_marked
         with 20 unmarked "errors" that are an artifact of this project having no baseline, not a rule this file means
         to prove. -->
    <IsPublicApiTracked>false</IsPublicApiTracked>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
